      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "PREFERRED SOLUTION: Build",
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "PREFERRED SOLUTION: Build",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1287",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 959,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 75.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0287",
      "seed": 19009,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 36731,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Build \u00b7 Belongs to the consuming project \u00b7 `gate.py --root <path>`, defaulting to\n`kit.ROOT` so every existing invocation is byte-identical; the library already takes\n`root` as a parameter everywhere, so only the CLI entry point pins it \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014\n`kit.py:22-24`'s own comment says the CLI passes ROOT and the selftest passes a temp tree,\nso the parameterisation is proven \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Build \u00b7 Belongs to the consuming project \u00b7 `gate.py --root <path>`, defaulting to\n`kit.ROOT` so every existing invocation is byte-identical; the library already takes\n`root` as a parameter everywhere, so only the CLI entry point pins it \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014\n`kit.py:22-24`'s own comment says the CLI passes ROOT and the selftest passes a temp tree,\nso the parameterisation is proven \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1288",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1046,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 90.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0288",
      "seed": 19016,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 36744,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Build \u00b7 Refusal from outside the model \u00b7 ship the checker in `tools/`, which the plugin\ncache already carries, and give it a locatable entry point so a consuming project's own CI\ncan invoke it \u00b7 temporary \u00b7 low \u2014 `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` is expanded nowhere in this repo\nand `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` measured unset in the tool environment; the script-location half\nis genuinely undesigned \u00b7 the first consuming project that runs the audit against itself,\nor the first release that ships a locatable entry point",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Build \u00b7 Refusal from outside the model \u00b7 ship the checker in `tools/`, which the plugin\ncache already carries, and give it a locatable entry point so a consuming project's own CI\ncan invoke it \u00b7 temporary \u00b7 low \u2014 `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}` is expanded nowhere in this repo\nand `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` measured unset in the tool environment; the script-location half\nis genuinely undesigned \u00b7 the first consuming project that runs the audit against itself,\nor the first release that ships a locatable entry point",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1289",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1148,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 75.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0289",
      "seed": 19023,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 36757,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Build \u00b7 Forward trace to code and tests \u00b7 adopt OpenFastTrace's comment-tag convention and\ncheck it with a stdlib parser; the `Piece:` trailer already carries the commit end of the\nchain \u00b7 temporary \u00b7 medium \u2014 the trailer shipped at v0.91.0 and has never been written, so\nthe mechanism is built but unproven \u00b7 the first work commit that should carry a trailer\nand does not",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Build \u00b7 Forward trace to code and tests \u00b7 adopt OpenFastTrace's comment-tag convention and\ncheck it with a stdlib parser; the `Piece:` trailer already carries the commit end of the\nchain \u00b7 temporary \u00b7 medium \u2014 the trailer shipped at v0.91.0 and has never been written, so\nthe mechanism is built but unproven \u00b7 the first work commit that should carry a trailer\nand does not",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1290",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1235,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 60.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0290",
      "seed": 19030,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 36770,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "StrictDoc \u00b7 The same files \u00b7 adopt the `.sdoc` format without requiring the tool \u2014 the\nfiles stay plain text and readable, and StrictDoc becomes optional producer-side tooling\nover them \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 byte-for-byte round-trip was verified, but `.sdoc` is not\nthe project's existing markdown and every product doc would need converting \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "StrictDoc \u00b7 The same files \u00b7 adopt the `.sdoc` format without requiring the tool \u2014 the\nfiles stay plain text and readable, and StrictDoc becomes optional producer-side tooling\nover them \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 byte-for-byte round-trip was verified, but `.sdoc` is not\nthe project's existing markdown and every product doc would need converting \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1291",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1307,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 45.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0291",
      "seed": 19037,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 36783,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "StrictDoc \u00b7 Machine-readable by stdlib \u00b7 write a stdlib parser against `.sdoc` rather than\nusing the JSON export, which requires the tool to run \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 the format is\nregular enough to parse, but this is work the adoption was meant to avoid \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "StrictDoc \u00b7 Machine-readable by stdlib \u00b7 write a stdlib parser against `.sdoc` rather than\nusing the JSON export, which requires the tool to run \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 the format is\nregular enough to parse, but this is work the adoption was meant to avoid \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1292",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1364,
      "width": 594.0,
      "height": 45.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0292",
      "seed": 19044,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 36796,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "StrictDoc \u00b7 Category disposition \u00b7 declare disposition as a custom grammar field and check\ncompleteness with Kerd's own checker \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014 custom grammar fields are a\ndocumented, working feature \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "StrictDoc \u00b7 Category disposition \u00b7 declare disposition as a custom grammar field and check\ncompleteness with Kerd's own checker \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 high \u2014 custom grammar fields are a\ndocumented, working feature \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1293",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1421,
      "width": 580.8000000000001,
      "height": 45.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0293",
      "seed": 19051,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 36809,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "StrictDoc \u00b7 Maintenance and survival \u00b7 pin the version and keep the register readable\nwithout the tool, so abandonment costs only the viewer \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 two-person\nproject, pre-1.0, with a documented history of breaking format migrations \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "StrictDoc \u00b7 Maintenance and survival \u00b7 pin the version and keep the register readable\nwithout the tool, so abandonment costs only the viewer \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 medium \u2014 two-person\nproject, pre-1.0, with a documented history of breaking format migrations \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1294",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1478,
      "width": 580.8000000000001,
      "height": 45.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0294",
      "seed": 19058,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 36822,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Doorstop \u00b7 The same files \u00b7 accept the `reqs/**/` tree as the register's declared home\nrather than annotating existing product docs \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 low \u2014 it is a parallel layout\nby design and cannot annotate `docs/product/<slug>.md` at all \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Doorstop \u00b7 The same files \u00b7 accept the `reqs/**/` tree as the register's declared home\nrather than annotating existing product docs \u00b7 permanent \u00b7 low \u2014 it is a parallel layout\nby design and cannot annotate `docs/product/<slug>.md` at all \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "t1295",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 1535,
      "width": 574.2,
      "height": 60.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0295",
      "seed": 19065,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 36835,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1785400000000,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "customData": {
        "gen": "kerd"
      },
      "roundness": null,
      "text": "Doorstop \u00b7 Claude Code friendly \u00b7 give the model the exact filename convention and the\nper-document `.doorstop.yml`, so capture is a Write to a computable path \u00b7 permanent \u00b7\nmedium \u2014 the UID is the filename, so the model must compute the next free number before\nwriting \u00b7 \u2014",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 6,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Doorstop \u00b7 Claude Code friendly \u00b7 give the model the exact filename convention and the\nper-document `.doorstop.yml`, so capture is a Write to a computable path \u00b7 permanent \u00b7\nmedium \u2014 the UID is the filename, so the model must compute the next free number before\nwriting \u00b7 \u2014",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
